def mindmap(d):
 s='<svg class="mindmap" viewBox="0 0 1000 440" role="img" aria-label="DBMS Day'+str(d['day'])+' concept map"><title>'+E(d['title'])+'</title><rect x="15" y="175" width="235" height="85" rx="12" fill="#176955"/><text x="132" y="222" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="23">DBMS · Day'+str(d['day'])+'</text>'
 for i,(t,a,b) in enumerate(d['map']):
  y=12+i*106;s+=f'<path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 {y+45} 385 {y+45}" fill="none" stroke="#7d9eae" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="385" y="{y}" width="600" height="92" rx="8" fill="#eef4f7" stroke="#a4bac4"/><text x="405" y="{y+27}" font-size="22" font-weight="600">{E(t)}</text><text x="405" y="{y+54}" font-size="18">{E(a)}</text><text x="405" y="{y+79}" font-size="18">{E(b)}</text>'
 return s+'</svg>'
def shell(title,s):return '<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>'+E(title)+' · Aleph</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/psets/material-page.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/calculus-review/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/dsa-review/style.css"><script defer src="/dsa-review/workspace.js"></script></head><body><main class="wrap">'+s+'</main></body></html>'
for d in D:
 day=d['day'];s=f'<nav><a href="index.html">← Three-week DBMS review</a> · <a href="/">Aleph uploads</a></nav><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Week1 · Day{day} of7 · GATE DA</p><h1>{E(d["title"])}</h1><p class="sub">{E(d["goal"])}</p><p>Reading anchor: {E(d["source"])}. Selected sections, not whole-book completion.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Today’s route</h2><p>After DBMS Round1, use these relative study days as a review. Read the concept exposition and two worked examples (about30–40 minutes), close them, then attempt the five practice/diagnostic questions (about25 minutes plus checking). Record the original attempt before opening worked review, then consolidate with the big picture and mind map. Timing is provisional; mark what you did not reach.</p><p>Classical algebra uses sets; SQL usually uses bags. Nulls, delete actions, B+ layouts, hierarchies and byte counts follow each question’s explicit assumptions. No calendar dates are assigned.</p><h3>What the exam asks you to do</h3><ul>'
 for e in d['evidence']:s+='<li><a href="'+e['url']+'">DA'+str(e['year'])+' Q'+str(e['question'])+'</a> · '+E(e['pattern'])+'</li>'
 s+='</ul><p>These links are pattern evidence. The practice below is original; the question numbering and official answer keys are not repurposed as answers to our variants.</p></section><section class="panel accent" id="review">'+d['story']+'</section><h2>Two worked examples</h2>'
 for title,prompt,answer in d['worked']:s+='<section class="panel"><h3>'+E(title)+'</h3><p>'+E(prompt)+'</p><p>'+E(answer)+'</p></section>'
 s+='<section class="panel" id="diagnostic"><h2>Exam-pattern practice and diagnostic</h2><p>Two multi-select questions and three short results/explanations. Ten points total:2 each; short responses receive1 for the result and1 for the requested reason. This is a learning diagnostic, not the official examination marking scheme. Select all correct options and no incorrect ones.</p><p id="status" role="status">Drafts and recorded attempts stay on this browser. Export and upload through the DBMS review subject for an Aleph submission.</p>'
 for x in d['questions']:
  ident=x['id'];s+=f'<article class="problem" data-question="{ident}" data-skill="{x["skill"]}"><h3>{ident} · {x["minutes"]} minutes</h3><p>{E(x["prompt"])}</p>'
  for j,opt in enumerate(x['options']):s+=f'<label class="option"><input type="checkbox" data-option="{ident}" value="{chr(65+j)}"> {E(opt)}</label>'
  s+=f'<label>Your reasoning<textarea data-answer="{ident}" rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Attempt status<select data-attempt="{ident}"><option value="">Choose</option><option>Attempted</option><option>Not attempted</option><option>Not reached</option></select></label><label>Confidence<select data-confidence="{ident}"><option value="">Not recorded</option><option>Low</option><option>Medium</option><option>High</option></select></label><label>Help or prior exposure<input type="text" data-help="{ident}" placeholder="None, hint used, or reference consulted"></label></article>'
 s+='<label class="confirm"><input type="checkbox" id="confirm-attempt"> I have recorded my attempt, including anything not reached.</label><button id="record-attempt" type="button">Record this attempt and open review</button><p>This records a frozen original on the current browser. It does not submit to Aleph; use the subject upload controls.</p></section><section class="panel" id="feedback" hidden><h2>Worked review</h2><p id="mcq-result"></p><p>Compare each original response with its key. Later corrections remain separate from the original attempt. The existing Aleph AI feedback flow is available after upload.</p>'
 for x in d['questions']:s+='<article><h3>'+x['id']+'</h3><p>'+E(x['answer'])+'</p><p><strong>First step:</strong> '+E(x['first'])+'. <strong>Diagnostic tag:</strong> '+E(x['skill'])+'. <strong>Likely trap:</strong> '+E(x['trap'])+'.</p></article>'
 s+='<h3>Targeted repair</h3><p>'+E(d['repair'])+'</p><h3>A fresh check</h3><p>'+E(d['retest'][0])+'</p><details><summary>Check after trying</summary><p>'+E(d['retest'][1])+'</p></details></section>'
 s+='<section class="panel" id="big-picture" hidden><h2>The big picture</h2><p>'+E(d['goal'])+' Reconstruct the main connections below, then explain one using your own small instance rather than repeating a definition.</p>'+mindmap(d)+'<details><summary>Text version of the mind map</summary><ul>'+''.join('<li><strong>'+E(t)+':</strong> '+E(a)+'; '+E(b)+'.</li>' for t,a,b in d['map'])+'</ul></details><label>Correction note: first broken step, next drill and fresh-check result<textarea data-correction="note" rows="4"></textarea></label></section>'
 s+='<section class="panel"><h2>Keep and submit your work</h2><button id="export" type="button">Export original and corrected work</button> <button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print current view</button><p>Upload the export or written solutions under <strong>Aleph → Subjects → DBMS: three-week review</strong>. Browser-local recording is not a server submission or a mastery claim.</p></section><nav>'+(f'<a href="day-{day-1:02}.html">← Previous day</a> · ' if day>1 else '')+(f'<a href="day-{day+1:02}.html">Next day →</a>' if day<7 else '<a href="index.html#week2">Next: Week2 plan</a>')+'</nav>'
 keys={x['id']:x['correct'] for x in d['questions'] if x['type']=='multi-select'}
 config={'storagePrefix':'aleph-dbms-review-v1','title':'DBMS review','exportPrefix':'dbms','uploadLabel':'Aleph DBMS review subject'}
 s+='<script>window.REVIEW_KEYS='+json.dumps(keys)+';window.REVIEW_CONFIG='+json.dumps(config)+';</script>'
 (R/f'day-{day:02}.html').write_text(shell(d['title'],s))
